  "body": "**Stacked on #1016 and #993** (merge order: #957, #993, #1016, then this). SKULL merged #993's branch in (aeff62af) because both change the cross-drill call lines in `operation/cross_spindle.rs`: kept #993's `cutter` arguments and this PR's ghost `map_err` on every line. Until the parents merge, this diff also shows their commits.\n\n**Stacked on #1016** (issue #871, branch `issue/871-refusal-ghost-rest`). Until #1016 merges, this diff also shows its commits. Only `78fd6e80` belongs to this PR. Retarget/merge order: #1016 first.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (mkinney/Camcraft, PROCESS_VERSION 16).\n\n## What changed\n\nThese are the part-way refusals #871 listed as owed. Each now hands back its partial path in the frame of the path the generator returns, so it lands where the part is once `run_job` maps that frame (none, or a 3+2 tilt through `world_path`). Where a generator plans in a frame of its own and maps out at the end, the ghost takes the same map the path takes. Success paths are untouched. Every change is a `map_err` on an error path, plus one new merge (`GenError::after_moves` / `Ghost::after`).\n\n| Site | Result |\n|---|---|\n| finishing3d raster: crossing pass, `rings_and_tail` (parallel, blend, radial, spiral, flow, shadow), `swarf_multi` rungs | **ghost in world** (moves built so far, output frame) |\n| finishing3d `waterline` (rings) | **ghost adopted**. Today only first-level refusals (non-finite facet, geo error) can reach it, so nothing shows yet |\n| Rotary Contour / Parallel: `waterline` / `swarf` on frame-local facets | **ghost in world**, via `rotary::to_world`. It goes through `posed`, the same pose law and world exit the finished path takes. A ghost `posed` refuses is dropped. The spot rides `f.to_world` |\n| Rotary links (`radial_relink`) | **ghost in world** (passes linked so far, carried out the same way) |\n| Rotary posing (`posed`) itself | **listed**: cycle or empty base (nothing to show), finite-horizon tail |\n| 5-axis stamp shank refusal (Multi-Axis Rough, Contour/Parallel/Flow 5D, swarf) | **ghost in world**: the plan before the refused move (world, unposed, so tips are within one ball radius of the posed ones). Posing a prefix is listed as dropped, with the reason |\n| Contour/Parallel/Swarf 5D: refusal inside the finishing plan | **ghost in world** (the plan's own, passed up) |\n| Swarf link laws (`link_swings`, `guard_turns`) | **ghost in world** (the posed path they judged). No fixture reaches these today |\n| Multi-axis curve walk (`contour_curve`) | **ghost in world** (chains walked before the refused one). `curve_walk::walk` itself holds rests, not moves (**listed**) |\n| Rotary gate (`stamp_spindle_c`) | **ghost in world** (the kernel path it judged) |\n| Rotary letter gate (`rotary_letter`) | **listed**: it runs before any move |\n| Fixture route (`plan_links` Unreachable) | **ghost in world** (upright mill, frame None) |\n| Cross drill `rapids_clear`, `cross_holder` | **ghost in world**: the spindle-frame chain moved back by the same `(ox, oy)` shift. A chain with arcs gets no ghost |\n| Cross drill `part_clear` | **ghost in world** (the world chain it judged) |\n| Nested: `pocket3d_air_split` material leg, `run_rest` rest ladder, stitched contour runs | **merged**: `after_moves` puts the outer moves in front of the inner ghost. Rotary Offset, the only air-split caller, still drops the ghost on purpose (development space) |\n| `run_rest`'s sim steps between the ladders | **listed** (not in the issue; could take `with_ghost(&coarse)` later) |\n| Face under an area turn | **handled by #1023** (`boundary_turn::turn_refusal` / `face_over_back`). `boundary_turn.rs` and the Face call sites are not touched here |\n\nThe decisions and reasons are in `docs/decisions/1015-ghost-frames.md`.\n\n## Tests (pinning)\n\n- `motion/tests/refusal_ghost_frames.rs` (new):\n  - `the_raster_refused_at_its_rings_hands_back_the_world_raster`: on an off-origin plate, the ghost equals the opening of the successful world path move for move. `parallel5d` hands back the same world plan.\n  - `the_rotary_parallel_ghost_rides_the_pose_law_to_the_world_bar`: on a bar laid off-origin, the ghost's cut tips lie on the world bar's skin and coincide (within 1e-6) with tips of the posted path. Nothing of the ghost stands inside the work.\n  - `a_refused_drive_curve_hands_back_the_chains_walked_before_it`: the ghost equals the lone first chain's path minus its closing retract. A first-chain refusal has no ghost.\n- `motion/tests/multiaxis_avoid.rs::the_shank_refusal_hands_back_the_world_plan_before_its_move`: the ghost is a prefix of the unposed world 3-D ladder.\n- `motion` lib: `ghost::tests::the_outer_moves_stand_in_front_and_a_bad_join_is_refused` and `gen_error::tests::a_nested_refusal_shows_the_outer_moves_then_its_own` (the Ghost merge).\n- `app` lib: `rotary_gate::tests::a_gate_refusal_hands_back_the_world_path_it_judged` and `cross_spindle::tests::an_app_side_law_refusal_carries_the_chain_to_the_world`.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on this head: green, all 4 steps (motion suites incl. refusal_ghost, refusal_ghost_frames, rotary, rotary_links, rotary_offset, pivot5d, flow, ruling, swarf_pose_continuity; app suites incl. refusal_ghost, drilling_cross_*, fixture_route, c_axis_*, center_cut_multiaxis; ui lib incl. refusal_ghost).\n- Extra: app golden_cl, conformance, solid_law_goldens, rotary_field_parity/fixtures/letter/verify; motion multiaxis, multiaxis_rough, swarf_reentry, multiaxis_avoid; clippy -D warnings on motion + app. all green (golden_cl 25, conformance 6, rotary_verify 9, ...; clippy clean).\n- **Goldens byte-identical**: no golden file changed, and golden_cl and conformance pass unchanged. No snapshot PNG touched.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `link_swings` / `guard_turns` refusals and `radial_relink`'s part-way lift refusal: no fixture reaches them. The wiring is the same one-liner the pinned sites use, over a path already in world.\n- The nested merges at their real sites (air-split material leg, rest ladder, stitched run): pinned by the merge unit tests only. No fixture refuses mid-leg.\n\nChangelog: A refusal that stops part-way through a rotary, 5-axis, curve, cross-drill, fixture-route, C-gate or nested (rest / air-split / stitched) generation now shows the path built so far where the part is (#1015)\n\nEffort: high (safety floor, display-only; no escalation)\n\nFixes #1015\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
